+# Authored HMMER input-format episode verification
+
+This packet adds only `tests/test_hmmer_alignment_input_episode_path.py` and
+files in this verification directory. It records authored tests and static
+inspection, not an executed native/integration result or completed inventory
+row. The original user attachment remains authoritative. No goal, scope
+amendment, production code, existing test, prompt, library, runner or progress
+file is changed.
+
+## Exact verification selection
+
+The whole new test file selects nine small cases: eight values of
+`test_declared_input_format_reaches_shared_sheet_return_and_saved_replay`, plus
+`test_original_source_alphabet_inference_reaches_return_and_saved_replay`.
+`TEST_SELECTORS.txt` lists the exact nine selectors. Do not collect or execute
+them on the host. Root owns execution through the existing packet 529 frozen
+lifecycle with 20 GiB RAM, 4 GiB scratch, zero swap and no wall cap. No producer
+fixture is regenerated and no completed Stockholm weighting/sampling case is
+selected by this file.
+
+Every selected operation is real `alimask alignment_to_model`, with selected
+`--fast --wgsc --seed 17 --fragthresh 0 --symfrac .6`. Eight cases select `--dna`
+and range `1-4`; the AFA inference case omits every alphabet flag and selects
+range `1-12`. Compiler-owned `--informat` retains the selected format. Existing
+scientific choices/controller are scripted engineering fixtures; native
+software identity, job, execution, capture, grading and result transport are
+production paths.
+
+## Authored inputs and expected numerical meanings
+
+All inputs are explicitly authored engineering operands, not original native
+emissions or biological measurements. Their exact bytes/hashes and expectations
+are in `FIXTURES.json`, extracted from literal test declarations without
+importing application code.
+
+| Declared format | Source representation of the three logical rows | Expected decoded rows |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| afa | FASTA names and uppercase rows | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+| a2m | AaaA, AaaA, CC; two consensus residues and a two-column insert slot | AaaA, AaaA, C--C |
+| psiblast | Physical AaaA, AaaA, C--C columns with consistent case | AaaA, AaaA, C--C |
+| selex | Third physical sequence uses two internal spaces | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+| clustal | Strict CLUSTAL header and a required all-space consensus line | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+| clustallike | Generic alignment header and a required all-space consensus line | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+| phylip | Header 3 4; exactly ten bytes per name | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+| phylips | Header 3 4; exactly ten bytes per name | AAAA, AAAA, C--C |
+
+All eight share the already-established GSC numerical example: weights
+`[0.75, 0.75, 1.5]`, MAP `[1,4]`, native selected range `1-4 -> 1-2`.
+A2M/PSI retain their case-derived RF `x..x`; the selected fast map keeps the same
+existing weighting/occupancy meaning. No second format-specific formula is
+implemented in the tests.
+
+The distinct inference input is AFA with rows `ACGTACGTACGT`,
+`ACGTACGTACGT`, `C--CC--CC--C`. The complete retained native
+`esl_msafile_afa_GuessAlphabet` and `esl_abc_GuessAlphabet` functions establish
+the authored expectation: EOF histogram A6 C12 G6 T6, total 30 (>10), all four
+canonical DNA letters and no outside-DNA letters; expected alphabet DNA.
+The expected GSC weights remain `[0.75,0.75,1.5]`, MAP is
+`[1,4,5,8,9,12]`, and native range `1-12 -> 1-6`. These are expected values
+pending root execution, not observed native results.
+
+Only these existing scalar paths and checks are requested in the returned
+row; the form contains exactly `completed` and `rows`:
+
+| Scalar | Meaning/unit | Eight-format expected value | Inference expected value |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| components.input_sequence_count | Captured source sequences; sequence_count | 3 | 3 |
+| components.input_column_count | Decoded source width; alignment_column_count | 4 | 12 |
+| components.mapped_model_position_count | Shared reconstructed match-position count; model_position_count | 2 | 6 |
+| components.native_mapping_row_count | Actual parsed native mapping rows; decoded_mapping_row_count | 1 | 1 |
+
+Requested checks are `native_mapping` and `requested_ranges`; both must pass.
+Returned values/state/unit must equal retained calculated cells exactly. The
+actual parsed native source/target range endpoints are checked independently.
+Original native weight annotations remain missing; calculated GSC weights do
+not masquerade as supplied WT annotations.
+
+## Required dependency stages
+
+The public harness ports remain unchanged and have been read completely:
+`tests/test_native_hmmer_preparation_contracts.py` (`job`, `operand`),
+`tests/test_native_hmmer_preparation_workflow.py` (`run_case`, `choice_for`,
+`assert_accounting`, `assert_native_custody`, `assert_projected_values`,
+`read_retained`, `forbid_work`), and
+`tests/test_hmmer_alignment_map_episode_path.py` (the existing weighting and
+closed replay pattern). No replacement runtime is implemented.
+
+| Stage | Existing implementation dependency and required output |
+| --- | --- |
+| Selected invocation | `native_hmmer_preparation_contracts.py:compile_native_hmmer_preparation_job`; exact format/options/software, no injected alphabet flag |
+| Real resource child | Existing Workflow launch/local/results children and `native_hmmer_preparation_local.py`; one chosen job and original attempt identity |
+| MAP safety | `native_hmmer_preparation_driver.py:_alimask_preflight_shared`; new-format source decoding/effective alphabet feed the shared first-record map |
+| Acquired original bytes | `native_hmmer_preparation_acquisition.py` and existing result worker; selected/staged/final source hashes equal authored input hash |
+| Input decoding | Root-owned `hmmer_alignment_preparation_data.py:read_hmmer_alignment_input` adapter and `hmmer_alignment_input_validation.py` over frozen 537/538/540/541 ports; original rows/RF feed the existing sheet |
+| Sheet | `hmmer_alignment_preparation_data.py:populate_hmmer_alignment_preparation_sheet`; schema remains hmmer_alignment_preparation_sheet_v1 |
+| Numerical authority | `hmmer_alignment_preparation_calculations.py:calculate_hmmer_alignment_preparation_components` and `reconstruct_alimask_model_map`; existing numerical meanings and map |
+| Saved-only calculation | `native_hmmer_preparation_worker.py:recalculate_hmmer_preparation`; one call of the same calculator, exact whole result equality |
+| Published/requested return | Existing result publication/views/typed return owner through `run_case`; chosen numerical cells and checks delivered to the scientific parent |
+| Closed replay | Existing saved results collector; original outcome/form/history/artifacts returned unchanged with all fresh scientific work forbidden |
+
+The tests hide both the original input path and native attempt before saved-only
+recalculation. They forbid all file opens, native start/status/wait, subprocess
+start, networking, acquisition, fresh grading, parser entrypoints and known
+imported decoder aliases. Saved histogram validation is allowed; original-byte
+alphabet inference is forbidden. A tracked wrapper verifies the existing shared
+calculator is called once and receives the same sheet/explicit parameters.
+
+Closed replay then additionally forbids the shared calculator, map reconstruction
+and saved recalculation (including loaded imported aliases). Only asyncio's local
+AF_UNIX wakeup socket is permitted. It compares the original returned operation,
+typed form, parent received facts, retained bundle/grade/sheet/calculation bytes,
+and every durable row in runtime_actions/runtime_observations/runtime_forms/
+runtime_episodes. One result child action contributes its existing acquisition
+credit 2; one parent unit contains that result child; the final expected gain is
+exact zero and root history remains `(0,0)`. No scientific Store observation is
+created by these preparation operations.
+
+## Static checks and outstanding ports
+
+Performed by this author: full listed harness/contracts/handoffs reading,
+relevant complete worker/data/calculator/compiler/journal functions and native
+alphabet classifier/scanner reading, stdlib AST syntax inspection, literal
